---

<section id="research" class="py-24 section-padding bg-dark-surface/30">
  <div class="content-max">
    <div class="reveal mb-12">
      <p class="text-amber font-mono text-sm tracking-wider mb-2">Publication</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-4">Research</h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary max-w-2xl">
        Published work at the intersection of medical imaging and artificial intelligence, 
        addressing healthcare challenges in resource-constrained environments.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="bg-dark-surface border border-border rounded-2xl overflow-hidden hover:border-amber/30 transition-all duration-300">
        <div class="p-8 md:p-10">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-6">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-amber/10 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
              <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-amber" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9.663 17h4.673M12 3v1m6.364 1.636l-.707.707M21 12h-1M4 12H3m3.343-5.657l-.707-.707m2.828 9.9a5 5 0 117.072 0l-.548.547A3.374 3.374 0 0014 18.469V19a2 2 0 11-4 0v-.531c0-.895-.356-1.754-.988-2.386l-.548-.547z"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-amber">Medical AI · Computer Vision · 2024</span>
              <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary mt-1 leading-tight">
                Domain-Adaptive Transformer for Data-Efficient Glioma Segmentation in Sub-Saharan MRI
              </h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-2">
                Ilerioluwakiiye Abolade, <strong>Aniekan Udo</strong>, Augustine Ojo, Abdulbasit Oyetunji, Hammed Ajigbotosho, Aondana Iorumbur, Confidence Raymond, Maruf Adewole
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-6 max-w-3xl">
            Glioma segmentation is critical for diagnosis and treatment planning, yet remains challenging in Sub-Saharan Africa due to limited MRI infrastructure and heterogeneous acquisition protocols that induce severe domain shift. We propose <strong>SegFormer3D-plus</strong>, a radiomics-guided transformer architecture designed for robust segmentation under domain variability.
          </p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-6 text-sm text-text-secondary">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber mt-0.5">01</span>
              <span>Histogram matching for intensity harmonization across scanners</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber mt-0.5">02</span>
              <span>Radiomic feature extraction with PCA-reduced k-means for domain-aware stratified sampling</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber mt-0.5">03</span>
              <span>Dual-pathway encoder with frequency-aware feature extraction and spatial-channel attention</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber mt-0.5">04</span>
              <span>Composite Dice-Cross-Entropy loss for boundary refinement</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-6 max-w-3xl">
            Pretrained on BraTS 2023 and fine-tuned on BraTS-Africa data, SegFormer3D-plus demonstrates improved tumor subregion delineation and boundary localization across heterogeneous African clinical scans, highlighting the value of radiomics-guided domain adaptation for resource-limited settings.
          </p>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-8">
            <span class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm bg-dark-elevated border border-border rounded-lg text-text-secondary">
              PyTorch
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm bg-dark-elevated border border-border rounded-lg text-text-secondary">
              Medical AI
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm bg-dark-elevated border border-border rounded-lg text-text-secondary">
              Computer Vision
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm bg-dark-elevated border border-border rounded-lg text-text-secondary">
              SegFormer3D-plus
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm bg-dark-elevated border border-border rounded-lg text-text-secondary">
              Radiomics
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm bg-dark-elevated border border-border rounded-lg text-text-secondary">
              Domain Adaptation
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
            <a 
              href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.02928"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-amber text-dark font-medium rounded-lg hover:bg-amber-hover transition-colors"
            >
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path d="M12 0C5.372 0 0 5.372 0 12s5.372 12 12 12 12-5.372 12-12S18.628 0 12 0zm0 2c5.514 0 10 4.486 10 10s-4.486 10-10 10S2 17.514 2 12 6.486 2 12 2zm-1 5v4H8v2h3v4h2v-4h3v-2h-3V7h-2z"/>
              </svg>
              Read Paper on arXiv
            </a>
            <a 
              href="https://github.com/Dr-Aniekan-Udo"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 border border-border text-text-secondary rounded-lg hover:border-amber hover:text-amber transition-colors"
            >
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path d="M12 0c-6.626 0-12 5.373-12 12 0 5.302 3.438 9.8 8.207 11.387.599.111.793-.261.793-.577v-2.234c-3.338.726-4.033-1.416-4.033-1.416-.546-1.387-1.333-1.756-1.333-1.756-1.089-.745.083-.729.083-.729 1.205.084 1.839 1.237 1.839 1.237 1.07 1.834 2.807 1.304 3.492.997.107-.775.418-1.305.762-1.604-2.665-.305-5.467-1.334-5.467-5.931 0-1.311.469-2.381 1.236-3.221-.124-.303-.535-1.524.117-3.176 0 0 1.008-.322 3.301 1.23.957-.266 1.983-.399 3.003-.404 1.02.005 2.047.138 3.006.404 2.291-1.552 3.297-1.23 3.297-1.23.653 1.653.242 2.874.118 3.176.77.84 1.235 1.911 1.235 3.221 0 4.609-2.807 5.624-5.479 5.921.43.372.823 1.102.823 2.222v3.293c0 .319.192.694.801.576 4.765-1.589 8.199-6.086 8.199-11.386 0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12z"/>
              </svg>
              View Code
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
